# Create a private Ethereum blockchain, create account, start mining, and check Ether balance.

Short Memorization Flow
Install → Create Folder → Create Genesis → Initialize → Create Account → Start Network → Attach Console → Mine & Check Balance
Step-by-Step Commands
Step 1: Install Geth
Download and install Geth  Geth file download (https://geth.ethereum.org/downloads/)
Add Geth path in Environment Variables C:\Program Files\Geth
Open CMD as Administratorgeth attach \\.\pipe\geth.ipc

Step 2: Create Data Folder

Create a folder:
mychaindata
Run - geth init genesis.json --datadir mychaindata



Step 3: Create genesis.json

Inside mychaindata, create a file named:

genesis.json

Paste:

{
  "config": {
    "chainId": 1234,
    "homesteadBlock": 0,
    "eip150Block": 0,
    "eip155Block": 0,
    "eip158Block": 0,
    "byzantiumBlock": 0,
    "constantinopleBlock": 0,
    "petersburgBlock": 0,
    "istanbulBlock": 0,
    "berlinBlock": 0,
    "londonBlock": 0,
    "terminalTotalDifficulty": 0
  },
  "difficulty": "1",
  "gasLimit": "8000000",
  "alloc": {}
}

Step 4: Initialize Blockchain

Run:

geth --datadir mychaindata init genesis.json

Purpose:

Creates Genesis Block
Initializes private blockchain

Step 5: Create Ethereum Account

Run:

geth account new --datadir mychaindata
Enter password
Account address gets generated

Step 6: Start Private Network

Run:
geth --datadir mychaindata --networkid 1234 --http --http.api "eth,net,web3,miner" --authrpc.jwtsecret mychaindata/geth/jwtsecret --mine --allow-insecure-unlock console

load it:
geth --datadir mychaindata --networkid 1234 --http --http.api eth,net,web3,miner,admin --allow-insecure-unlock console

Purpose:

Starts private Ethereum blockchain

Step 7: Open Geth JS Console

Open new CMD and run:

geth attach \\.\pipe\geth.ipc

Step 8: Check Accounts

Inside console:

eth.accounts

Shows Ethereum account address.

Step 9: Start Mining

Run:

miner.start()

Purpose:

Starts mining Ether
Creates blocks

Stop mining:

miner.stop()
Step 10: Check Ether Balance

Run:

web3.fromWei(eth.getBalance(eth.accounts[0]), "ether")

Shows mined Ether balance.
